Reject export records with undefined or malformed references instead of panicking

The name and level record decoders indexed their tables directly and
unwrapped field values: a name whose "pre" is not yet defined panicked
with index out of bounds (parser.rs handle_name), as did a level, sort or
universe argument naming an undefined level (level_at), and a "succ",
"param", "sort" or "bvar" value that is not a number hit unwrap() on
None. These now reject like the expression decoder already does for an
undefined expression index ("... index N is out of range" / "field `k`
must be a u32"). The first was found by a wasmfuzz smoke run within
seconds (repro in suite-repros); the others are the same pattern next to
it. Regression test in tests/exports.rs.
Upstream: none (no related issue or PR; open issues #3 and #5 are
soundness reports, checked 2026-11-22).

